The CustomerId column in the Customer table does not have a default sequence (serial or identity) for auto-increment. We need to manually assign CustomerId starting from the next available ID.

I will find the current max CustomerId, then insert the customer data with incremented CustomerId values starting from max + 1, assigning SupportRepId = 3 and Fax as NULL, using an efficient bulk insert operation.
| execute_sql {"sql": "INSERT INTO public.\"Customer\" (\"CustomerId\", \"FirstName\", \"LastName\", \"Company\", \"Address\", \"City\", \"State\", \"Country\", \"PostalCode\", \"Phone\", \"Fax\", \"Email\", \"SupportRepId\")\nSELECT\n    (SELECT MAX(\"CustomerId\") FROM public.\"Customer\") + ROW_NUMBER() OVER () AS \"CustomerId\",\n    FirstName,\n    LastName,\n    Company,\n    Address,\n    City,\n    State,\n    Country,\n    PostalCode,\n    Phone,\n    NULL AS Fax,\n    Email,\n    3 AS \"SupportRepId\"\nFROM staging_customer;"}
